    description: "Found in DEEP bakeoff deep-20260623-134237 cohort-001 iter-004 (pretix, Django/Celery). io-boundaries reports total_io_edges=191/101342 (0.19%) because the boundary taxonomy (env_read, logging, fs_read/write, subprocess, net_send/recv, browser_storage, command_launch) has NO db_* category and weak net/cache primitives. Source reality invisible to the detector: 4991 '.objects.', 2632 '.save()', 305 'transaction.atomic', 305 cursor.execute/.raw (DB); 128 'cache.*' + 1005 redis refs (cache); 23 'requests.*' + 58 send_mail/smtplib (net_send=2, only socket.connect caught). Drives the LOW_IO_TAG_RATE WARNs across the whole cohort (express/apollo/caddy/pretix all flagged). Also a FALSE POSITIVE: net_recv tags django.core.management.execute_from_command_line (a CLI dispatcher, not network I/O). FIX: add db_read/db_write boundary categories + Django-ORM / SQLAlchemy / cache(redis) / requests / smtplib entries to the io_primitives catalogs; fix the execute_from_command_line net_recv FP. Repro: hypergumbo io-boundaries on a Django repo."  # 9422
